---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import ButtonLink from '../components/ButtonLink.astro';
import { contact } from '../data/contact';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Meet Evan Lebrecht and learn how clear communication, practical problem-solving, and hands-on development shape Calypso Digital Studio."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="About the studio"
    title="I build by understanding the business before choosing the solution."
    description="Calypso Digital Studio combines thoughtful design, practical development, and a direct working relationship with the person building your project."
  />

  <section class="about container">
    <div class="about__story">
      <p class="eyebrow">The person behind the work</p>
      <h2>Practical problem-solving, shaped by hands-on experience.</h2>
      <p>
        I’m Evan Lebrecht, the designer and developer behind Calypso Digital Studio.
        My background includes customer-facing work, team leadership, independent
        software projects, and hands-on responsibility for solving problems with
        limited time and resources.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those experiences taught me to listen closely, explain complicated
        requirements in plain language, organize scattered information, and keep a
        project moving when the path is not obvious.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not assume an existing process is the best process. I look at what
        customers need, where a workflow slows down, what information is missing,
        and what can be made clearer or more efficient. That approach guides every
        website and custom tool I build.
      </p>
      <p>
        The studio is based in New York’s Capital Region and works with clients
        anywhere.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="about__brand surface">
      <img
        src="/assets/brand/calypso-master.webp"
        alt="Calypso Digital Studio illustrated logo"
        width="1200"
        height="1200"
      />
      <figcaption>
        The studio is named after Calypso. Her markings and personality shaped
        the warm, organic identity without turning the business into a novelty brand.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="mindset container">
    <header class="mindset__intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I approach the work</p>
      <h2>The goal is not to sell the most features. It is to build what the business will actually use.</h2>
      <p>
        I focus on what a project needs to accomplish in real use: what customers
        must understand, what the owner needs to manage, where the current process
        creates friction, and what will still make sense after launch.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mindset__grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Business-first recommendations</h3>
        <p>
          Recommendations come from the business goals, customer journey, and actual
          workflow—not from trends, templates, or a platform I am trying to sell.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Plain-language communication</h3>
        <p>
          Clients should understand what is being built, why it matters, and what
          decisions still need to be made.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Practical functionality</h3>
        <p>
          Every page and feature should help a customer take action, reduce
          confusion, or make the business easier to run.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Clear accountability</h3>
        <p>
          Scope, limitations, progress, and recommendations should stay clear
          throughout the project—even when the honest answer is that a feature is
          unnecessary.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-card container surface">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact Evan</p>
      <h2>Have a business problem that may need a website or custom tool?</h2>
      <p>
        Email is the most direct way to begin. You can also follow the studio and
        see current work through its social profiles.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-card__links">
      <a class="contact-card__email" href={contact.emailHref}>{contact.email}</a>
      <a href={contact.instagram.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        {contact.instagram.label}
      </a>
      <a href={contact.facebook.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        {contact.facebook.label}
      </a>
      <ButtonLink href="/start">Start Your Project</ButtonLink>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .about__story p:not(.eyebrow) {
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .about__brand {
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about__brand figcaption {
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .mindset {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
  }

  .mindset__intro {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .mindset__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .mindset__grid article {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .contact-card {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-block: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }

  .contact-card__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .contact-card__links > a:not(.button) {
    font-weight: 800;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-rust);
    text-decoration-thickness: 0.12em;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .contact-card__email {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .mindset__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.75fr;
    }

    .contact-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
      padding: var(--space-7);
    }
  }
</style>
